WEBVTT

00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:15,820
My diet recommendations, you said, to stay away from bone broth because it's high in glutamine

00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:19,820
and also to stay away from high histamine foods.

00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:28,820
I'm trying to heal my gut right now and I'm looking at a vegan pea protein that contains glutamic acid and histidine.

00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,820
I'm not sure if they're the same as glutamine and histamine.

00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:38,820
Well, histidine is not the same as histamine and glutamic acid will convert to glutamine.

00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:45,820
So you could say glutamic acid and glutamine are the same, histidine and histamine are not the same.

00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:50,820
But so you can't use this so I wouldn't do that.

00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:59,820
Now, if a person, okay, so should every cancer patient stay away from glutamine in their supplements?

00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:03,820
The answer in my book would be yes.

00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:11,820
Unless the person is in a state of, you know, their cancer is in a state of remission.

00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:17,820
They've been doing really well and they want to do glutamine to heal their gut for a short period of time.

00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:23,820
That I'd say that's, I'm sure you're most likely going to be fine with that.

00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:34,820
It would be, you know, contraindicated if the person is going to go on a glutamine supplement for a longer period of time.

00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:44,820
Now, most good practitioners that are working at healing somebody's gut don't necessarily put them on high-dose glutamine for a long period of time anyhow.

00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:51,820
So a couple of weeks on a higher dose glutamine to try to heal the gut can be beneficial.

00:01:51,820 --> 00:02:00,820
This glutamine heals the gut because it stimulates growth, stimulates growth, regrowth of new epithelial cells that lie in the gut.

00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:06,820
So it helps grow new cells while it helps grow new cells.

00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:09,820
You have cancer cells in the gut or something too.

00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,820
So it also depends slightly on the type of cancer.

00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:21,820
If the person was dealing with colon cancer and they might be in full remission from colon cancer, I don't think I'd ever use glutamine.

00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:31,830
But if they're dealing, if they had breast cancer and they're in full remission, then I think using glutamine for a short period of time is fine.

00:02:31,830 --> 00:02:38,830
There's other things a person can do to heal their gut without using glutamine.

00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:50,830
So there's tons of different herbs that are gut healing herbs that are not going to stimulate growth too, so something to look into those things too.

